WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.069
The Marvel Cinematic Universe is built on
the performances of its superstar actors.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:06.069
So why did Chris Evans decide to quit?

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:09.430
Why can't Gwyneth Paltrow even remember the
movies she's already been in?

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:10.520
Keep watching to find out.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.000
Yes, we know, Iron Man is dead.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.779
But one thing we all know about comic book
movies is that nobody ever really stays dead.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:22.519
Hey, if they brought Gamora back, they can
bring Tony Stark back, right?

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:23.519
Well, maybe.

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:28.930
In 2017, Robert Downey Jr. told news.com.au
that he didn't want to stay in the MCU much

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:29.930
longer, saying,

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.780
"I just want to hang up my jersey before it's
embarrassing."

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:38.370
And then the character got the biggest sendoff
ever in 2019's "Avengers: Endgame."

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.620
So it seemed like Downey was done for good.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.789
Of his decision to leave, he told Howard Stern
in 2019,

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:47.850
"I didn't expect it to become what it became."

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.390
And also, I've always had other interests."

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:54.220
Despite this, Downey has still opened the
door for a possible return.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:59.670
In February, 2021, GQ asked Downey if he would
ever return, and Downey said, quote, "Never

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.670
say never."

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.039
Please come back, Tony!

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:04.468
We love you 3000!

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.729
Chris Evans, much like pal Robert Downey Jr.,
appears to be done with his MCU character

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:13.330
Steve Rogers - a.k.a. Captain America - and
hasn't expressed much interest in showing

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.890
up in the MCU again after "Avengers: Endgame."

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.240
Steve's story rounded out so nicely and he
got the happy ending he wanted with Peggy

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.350
Carter, which was ultra-satisfying to Evans.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.790
Despite that, he has still left the door open
for a return if the story is good enough.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:31.070
In 2019, he said in a Variety conversation
with Scarlett Johansson,

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.590
"If you're going to revisit it, it can't be
a cash grab.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.299
It can't be just because the audience wants
to be excited.

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:39.299
What are we revealing?

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.759
What are we adding to the story?

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:44.070
A lot of things would have to come together."

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.840
"Avengers…"

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.935
"...assemble!"

00:01:51.935 --> 00:01:57.360
Someone who has not been shy about his desire
to stay in the MCU is Chris Hemsworth.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.689
The actor has been playing Thor since 2011,
and if it were up to him, the ride would never

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.689
end.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:08.560
Hemsworth is the only MCU star with a fourth
solo film in the works, and if he has anything

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.039
to say about it, it won't be his last.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:16.140
In 2020 he told Elle Man that he's going to
keep going beyond the next Thor film, "Love

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.140
and Thunder."

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.480
"I'm not going into any retirement period.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.280
Thor is far too young for that.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.590
(He) is only 1500 years old!

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.790
It is definitely not a film that I say goodbye
to this brand."

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.349
Benedict Cumberbatch may not have as many
appearances under his belt as co-stars like

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:36.560
Robert Downey Jr. and Chris Hemsworth, but
his character Doctor Strange will play a major

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.530
part in the MCU going forward.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.480
Thankfully, Cumberbatch is excited about getting
to continue to play Stephen Strange and wants

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.770
to keep doing so for a long time.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.300
When speaking with Deadline back in 2018,
right after "Avengers: Infinity War" landed

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.520
in theaters, he was asked about playing Doctor
Strange in the future, to which he replied,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.440
"Just try to stop me."

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.180
After helping to save the day in" Avengers:
Endgame," he’s returned in "Spider-Man:

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.520
No Way Home" and will do so again next year
in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.299
— and hopefully long after.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:11.700
Tom Holland came slinging into our lives as
Spider-Man in 2016's "Captain America: Civil

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.940
War," followed by two solo and two Avengers
films.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.860
He completes the trilogy with "Spider-Man:
No Way Home," which debuted in the end of

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:19.860
2021.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.660
It also ends his contract with Marvel Studios.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:27.110
No need to worry though, as Holland is planning
on staying in the MCU for as long as they'll

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.160
let him.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.090
Contracts are extended all the time, and the
actor is ready to sign on the line.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.959
When catching up with Collider in early 2021,
he made sure to note that he wanted to don

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:38.810
the suit for as long as possible.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.950
"I've always said to them if they want me
back I'll be there in a heartbeat.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.610
I've loved every minute of being a part of
this amazing world.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.080
It's changed my life for the better, I'm so
lucky to be here.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.860
If they want me back I'll be there, if they
don't I will walk off into the sunset a very,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.790
very happy person because it's been an amazing
journey."

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.590
Clint Barton has been with the MCU for quite
some time now and has outlasted countless

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.610
foes despite only using a bow and arrow.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.800
Despite his lengthy stay with Marvel, he's
actually only had a major role in four films

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.000
and one small cameo in "Thor."

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.100
He also stars in his own Disney+ series, "Hawkeye,"
which debuted in November 2021, but Renner

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.600
might be done with his character after that.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.610
Back in 2017, the actor was asked by the South
China Morning Post about a potential Hawkeye

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.610
movie.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:31.440
While he expressed excitement and optimism
about the possibility, he said he would want

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:37.410
it to happen sooner rather than later because,
quote, "I don't want to be in my 50s in tights."

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.300
He's in his 50s now, so unless he's had a
change of heart, this might be it for Renner.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.530
We first met Sam Wilson in "Captain America:
The Winter Soldier," and he instantly won

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:51.310
over our hearts thanks to a brilliant portrayal
by Anthony Mackie.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.960
Sam has five major MCU appearances — in
addition to one small "Ant-Man" cameo — and

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.790
his own Disney+ series.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.230
At the conclusion of that six episode run,
he takes up the mantle as the new Captain

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.600
America– so we’ll surely be seeing him
again soon.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.050
In a digital press event for "Falcon and the
Winter Soldier," Mackie revealed that he would

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:14.160
love to appear somewhere in the upcoming Blade
film, even if it was just one line.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.060
He also said he would love to pop up in the
She-Hulk series, which is set to land on Disney+

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.060
in 2022.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.420
It’s been confirmed that Captain America
will return, with Mackie at the helm for the

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.440
foreseeable future.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.560
Paul Bettany has portrayed Vision for three
MCU films and one Disney+ series, and fans

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.660
have fallen in love with the synthezoid.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.400
Bettany has as well and is adamant about playing
the character for as long as Kevin Feige will

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.400
let him.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.940
In a March 2021 interview with Esquire, when
Bettany was asked if he was going to play

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.210
Vision forever, he said,

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.550
"I love Vision.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.270
Yes, I'm in."

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:52.100
We likely haven't seen the last of Vision
either, if the finale of "WandaVision" is

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.120
any indication.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:58.470
White Vision is currently on the loose, with
the original's memories but not the same personality.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:03.240
We'd be shocked to never see him again in
the MCU and are hoping Bettany really does

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.640
get to play the multi-dimensional character
again.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.410
Colonel James Rhodes has been in the MCU since
Day 1, appearing in "Iron Man" as Tony Stark's

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.410
best friend.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:16.860
The role was originally held by Terrence Howard,
but he left the franchise after a pay dispute.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.150
Don Cheadle replaced the actor in "Iron Man
2," making him one of the longest-tenured

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.220
actors in the MCU.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.970
Rhodey has mostly been a supporting character
for the last 11 years, but he will finally

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:32.240
get his chance to shine in his own Disney+
series, "Armor Wars," which is currently without

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.240
a release date.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.250
During a press tour in 2020, Cheadle mentioned
wanting to see Rhodey do different things

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:41.160
in the future, verifying in the process that
he still wants to play the role.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:45.750
"I'd really want to dig into him and maybe
even find something that felt closer to the

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.720
first Iron Man for who he was.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.030
[...] I think they can go anywhere with him
now."

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.270
Just like Don Cheadle, Mark Ruffalo almost
wasn't in the MCU.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.270
The Golden Globe winner took on the role of
Bruce Banner, a.k.a.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:01.880
The Hulk, in 2012's "The Avengers," after
Edward Norton stepped away following 2008's

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.270
"The Incredible Hulk."

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.941
In a 2020 interview with Variety, Ruffalo
noted how shocked and lucky he is that he

00:07:07.941 --> 00:07:13.160
gets to play the big green hero, and constantly
reminds himself of that when he's shooting

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.380
a Marvel film.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.480
After admitting that he can sometimes get
annoyed on set when things are taking too

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.860
long to set up, he revealed that he'll say
to himself,

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.560
"Hey, remember you're not even supposed to
be here."

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:28.030
He also suggested that he'd love to play Banner
for as long as they'll let him.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:32.370
And we know he's not done yet with the character
either, as he's confirmed to appear in the

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:33.470
Disney+ series "She-Hulk."

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:40.080
Another MCU star who doesn't plan on going
anywhere anytime soon is Star-Lord himself,

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.080
Chris Pratt.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:45.440
The "Guardians of the Galaxy" star is slated
to appear in at least two more MCU films that

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:51.740
we know of, "Thor: Love and Thunder" in 2022
and "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" in 2023.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:56.470
We don't know how many films he's under contract
for, but that doesn't seem to matter anyway.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:58.210
He told Slashfilm in 2017,

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:03.060
"I'll tell you, as much as I love Marvel,
it doesn't matter how many I have contracted

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.500
because I'm going to continue to work with
them.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.690
[...] I love working with them and I'm going
to continue to work with them whether they

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:10.710
like it or not.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:14.350
Even if they write me out, I'm going to show
up on set and be like, 'Hey, man!'

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.350
They're done.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.350
They don't get to shake me."

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:21.430
When it comes to "most appearances in MCU
films," you can put Gwyneth Paltrow toward

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.500
the top of the list with seven.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:28.570
Pepper Potts has been in every Iron Man film,
as well as "Spider-Man: Homecoming" and three

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:34.010
out of four Avengers flicks, but had relatively
minor roles for her last several appearances.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.409
It turns out this is just how she likes it.

00:08:36.409 --> 00:08:39.240
She isn't too crazy about spending a lot of
time on movie sets anymore.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.590
When it comes to the MCU, however, Paltrow
said she would be happy to show up to work

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:47.610
on a future project, just as long as it only
took a few days.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:51.400
Speaking with People in early 2021, the actress
said she would be open to returning to the

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.350
MCU, if it wasn't anything big.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:57.580
"I think if it was a small part that I could
do in like a day or two."

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.880
Not that she'll remember it anyway.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.880
"Spiderman?"

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:01.960
"Yeah, we were in Spiderman together.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.794
Remember we were in Spiderman?"

00:09:03.794 --> 00:09:04.794
"We weren't in Spiderman!"

00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:05.794
"Yes we were."

00:09:06.503 --> 00:09:11.220
One of the newer heroes in the MCU, Valkyrie,
has proven herself a force to be reckoned

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.220
with.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:16.310
With just two Marvel Studios films under her
belt, actress Tessa Thompson has a lot she

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.280
wants to prove in the Marvel franchise.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:22.460
She will appear in the fourth Thor flick due
out in 2022, but she wants to stick around

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:26.740
as long as possible to hopefully land in an
all-female team-up adventure.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.120
When she was just starting out with the MCU
in 2017, Thompson said at a press event that

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:35.860
she asked Kevin Feige about making an all-female
movie at the studio, and he apparently told

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.860
her yes.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:41.150
It's now four years later and we still have
no confirmation of one, but Thompson seems

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:43.990
like she wants to stick with the MCU until
it happens.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.760
She told CinemaBlend in 2019,

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:51.150
"There's so many incredible, talented women
in the MCU that I just want to work with selfishly."

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.310
Keep fighting the good fight, Valkyrie, because
we'd all love to see it too.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:00.280
No one has more appearances in the MCU than
Mr. Samuel L. Jackson.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.660
The legendary actor appeared in the first
"Iron Man" film's end credits and has been

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.680
popping up in movie after movie ever since.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:13.560
Jackson has shown up in 11 of 23 MCU films
— a healthy mix of supporting roles and

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.560
cameos.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.710
One of the older actors in the MCU, Jackson
isn't going to let age affect him moving forward.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:22.610
When speaking with The Hollywood Reporter
in 2019, Jackson said he would be happy to

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:24.640
play Nick Fury in his 80s, saying,

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.470
"I could be the Alec Guinness of Marvel movies."

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:32.030
He isn't going anywhere either, as he will
also be getting his own Disney+ series – "Secret

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:36.450
Invasion" – but whether he shows up in the
MCU anywhere else remains to be seen.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:41.530
It would be hard to imagine a world where
Fury didn't pop up in someone's post-credits

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.950
scene every now and again.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:48.800
"How I Met Your Mother" alum Cobie Smulders
joined the MCU in 2012 for "The Avengers"

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.710
as Nick Fury's right hand agent, and has since
popped up in five more MCU films.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:58.720
But while she doesn't have the same MCU resume
as other actors on our list, she definitely

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.230
has the same amount of passion as they do.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:05.390
When asked by The Hollywood Reporter in 2019
if she'd want to play Agent Maria Hill for

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.330
the rest of her life, the actress said,

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.120
"I would love to!

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.460
[...] I love being a part of the world of
Marvel.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:18.520
It's a magical, wonderful place filled with
only nice, caring, considerate, creative people."

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.600
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:23.570
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:27.210
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

